Next Step — N-Queens :   LeetCode 51
              
              Given an n × n chessboard, place n queens so that no two queens attack each other.              
              A queen attacks another queen if they share:
                                          same row
                                          same column
                                          same diagonal

            For:   n = 4
            
            one valid arrangement is:            
                                      . Q . .
                                      . . . Q
                                      Q . . .
                                      . . Q .
            
            We return the corresponding board representation.
================================================================================================================================================
Why N-Queens is important for your L6 preparation:

            This problem combines several things you've already learned:

                                      Backtracking
                                          ↓
                                      State design
                                          ↓
                                      Constraint checking
                                          ↓
                                      Pruning
                                          ↓
                                      Efficient mutable state



================================================================================================================================================
But there is an important upgrade.

                In Word Search, we asked:                
                            “Is this particular next move valid?”
                
                For N-Queens, we want to answer that question in O(1) rather than scanning the board every time.                
                That leads us toward:               
                                        sets
                                        +
                                        diagonal indexing
                                        +
                                        bitmasks
                
                and that is exactly the kind of optimization conversation I want you comfortable with at L6.

